  "notes": [
    "Prototype contract; not an operational national yield model.",
    "Assortment sorts are dimension-only; no official BC grade is assigned.",
    "BTC grade shares are context only.",
    "Fail-closed on unexpected git deletions.",
    "Expansion factors are fixed to the BTC target TPH and a positive diameter multiplier is solved by a bracketed root search so the taper total still equals the BTC target volume; height is recomputed from the scaled DBH.",
    "Weibull-containing mixtures are fitted on the left-truncated grouped support; new-family unstable fits are reported but not selected, while the legacy two-gamma fallback may remain selected and is flagged.",
    "Spike families are attempted only when the first DBH bin exceeds the documented share or the best simple fit leaves a high KS. The spike carries the first bin and the continuous tail starts at the first bin upper edge; the spike weight is an AIC parameter and does not set the volume scale. Unconstrained spike rows are audit-only and are never synthesis-eligible because their untruncated tail mean can be infinite. Constrained spike tails use a bounded grouped MLE (shape >= 1, scale >= 0.1 cm); a fit at any bound is reported as boundary_reject and is not selected."
  ],
